{
  "export_version": "1.0",
  "exported_at": "2026-08-26T13:12:15.503996+00:00",
  "use_case": {
    "name": "Issue Intake & Triage",
    "description": "Triage a Teams issue report (text + screenshots), draft a ticket, get human Approve/Reject in Teams, then create it.",
    "interface_type": "form",
    "workflow_json": {
      "version": "1.0",
      "activities": [
        {
          "id": "_start",
          "next": "triage",
          "type": "start",
          "config": {
            "input_schema": {
              "type": "object",
              "required": [
                "message"
              ],
              "properties": {
                "sender": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "channel": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "message": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "screenshots": {
                  "type": "array",
                  "items": {
                    "type": "image"
                  },
                  "maxItems": 5
                },
                "conversation_id": {
                  "type": "string"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "triage",
          "next": "route",
          "type": "agent",
          "config": {
            "name": "Issue Triage (vision)",
            "role": "Support issue triager",
            "agent_id": "8c99d5cd-1378-4276-af05-e261f1fa5884",
            "max_tokens": 4096,
            "input_fields": {
              "message": {
                "type": "string",
                "source": "input.message"
              },
              "screenshots": {
                "type": "image",
                "source": "input.screenshots"
              }
            },
            "instructions": "You triage messages from a support Teams channel. You are given the message text and, when the reporter pasted them, one or more screenshots.\n\nAbout the screenshots field: when the reporter attached images you will SEE them as vision content and must read them. The text `screenshots` field is only a side note: if it is empty or contains a placeholder such as \"[Error loading file: ...]\", it just means NO image was attached. Never treat that placeholder as evidence, never mention it, and never let it change the verdict. Triage from the text alone in that case.\n\nRead BOTH the text and every actual screenshot together. Screenshots often carry the real signal: error dialogs, stack traces, failed screens, red banners, HTTP 4xx/5xx codes, and UI glitches all count as evidence of a problem.\n\nDecide one verdict:\n- issue: a genuine, specific bug/incident/problem report with enough detail to act on (what broke, where, and ideally when or how).\n- needs_info: it sounds like a real problem but is too vague to log (\"it is broken again\", \"not working\") with no system, no error, and no steps.\n- noise: casual chat, greetings, thanks, opinions, questions that are not problem reports.\n\nWhen in doubt between issue and noise, prefer noise. When it sounds like a problem but lacks specifics, choose needs_info rather than inventing detail.\n\nFill every output field. For noise, still return short placeholder values (verdict=noise). Base severity on real user impact: critical=outage/data loss, high=major feature broken for many, medium=broken for some or has a workaround, low=minor/cosmetic. affected_area is a short slug like \"billing/export\" or \"auth/login\". title is a short ticket title. summary is one clean line describing the problem, incorporating anything you saw in the screenshots. reason is one line explaining the verdict.",
            "output_fields": {
              "verdict": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "Exactly one of: issue, needs_info, noise"
              },
              "title": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "Short ticket title"
              },
              "summary": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "One clean line describing the problem, including any screenshot insight"
              },
              "category": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "One of: bug, incident, feature_request, question"
              },
              "severity": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "One of: critical, high, medium, low (based on user impact)"
              },
              "affected_area": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "Short area slug, e.g. billing/export or auth/login"
              },
              "reason": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "One line explaining the verdict (auditable)"
              }
            },
            "max_iterations": 10,
            "kb_retrieval_mode": "auto",
            "enabled_system_tools": []
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "route",
          "type": "conditional",
          "config": {
            "condition_type": "variable",
            "variable_path": "triage.verdict",
            "operator": "match",
            "branches": [
              {
                "goto": "build_draft",
                "label": "issue"
              },
              {
                "goto": "build_clarify",
                "label": "needs_info"
              },
              {
                "goto": "noise_end",
                "label": "noise"
              }
            ],
            "default_branch": "noise"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "build_draft",
          "next": "approval",
          "type": "code",
          "config": {
            "name": "Build ticket draft",
            "code": "def run(inputs: Inputs) -> Outputs:\n    severity = (inputs.severity or \"\").strip().lower()\n    priority_sla = {\n        \"critical\": (\"P1\", \"2h\"),\n        \"high\": (\"P2\", \"4h\"),\n        \"medium\": (\"P3\", \"24h\"),\n        \"low\": (\"P4\", \"72h\"),\n    }\n    priority, sla = priority_sla.get(severity, (\"P3\", \"24h\"))\n\n    signal = ((inputs.affected_area or \"\") + \" \" + (inputs.category or \"\")).lower()\n    if any(k in signal for k in (\"export\", \"billing\", \"payment\", \"invoice\")):\n        owner = \"Billing squad\"\n    elif any(k in signal for k in (\"auth\", \"login\", \"sso\")):\n        owner = \"Platform squad\"\n    elif any(k in signal for k in (\"ui\", \"render\", \"frontend\")):\n        owner = \"Frontend squad\"\n    else:\n        owner = \"Triage / Support\"\n\n    title = (inputs.title or \"Untitled issue\").strip()\n    summary = (inputs.summary or \"\").strip()\n    category = (inputs.category or \"bug\").strip()\n    sev = severity or \"medium\"\n\n    preview = \"\\n\".join([\n        \"\ud83e\udd16 Proposed ticket (approval needed)\",\n        \"Title:    \" + title,\n        \"Category: \" + category + \"   |   Severity: \" + sev\n        + \"   |   Priority: \" + priority + \"   |   SLA: \" + sla,\n        \"Owner:    \" + owner,\n        \"Summary:  \" + summary,\n        \"\",\n        \"Reply Approve to create this ticket, or Reject to discard.\",\n    ])\n    return {\n        \"title\": title,\n        \"summary\": summary,\n        \"category\": category,\n        \"severity\": sev,\n        \"priority\": priority,\n        \"sla\": sla,\n        \"owner\": owner,\n        \"preview\": preview,\n    }\n",
            "input_fields": {
              "title": {
                "type": "string",
                "source": "triage.title"
              },
              "summary": {
                "type": "string",
                "source": "triage.summary"
              },
              "category": {
                "type": "string",
                "source": "triage.category"
              },
              "severity": {
                "type": "string",
                "source": "triage.severity"
              },
              "affected_area": {
                "type": "string",
                "source": "triage.affected_area"
              }
            },
            "output_fields": {
              "title": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "Ticket title"
              },
              "summary": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "One-line problem summary"
              },
              "category": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "Ticket category"
              },
              "severity": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "Severity level"
              },
              "priority": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "Derived priority P1-P4"
              },
              "sla": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "Derived SLA window"
              },
              "owner": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "Routed owning squad"
              },
              "preview": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "Teams-facing draft text"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "approval",
          "next": "reply_rejected",
          "type": "human_task",
          "config": {
            "name": "Approve ticket",
            "task_type": "approval",
            "title": "Approve support ticket",
            "description": "A triaged ticket is awaiting approval before it is created.",
            "assignee_id": "{{system.user_id}}",
            "context_fields": {
              "draft": {
                "source": "build_draft.preview",
                "label": "Proposed ticket"
              },
              "title": {
                "source": "build_draft.title",
                "label": "Title"
              },
              "summary": {
                "source": "build_draft.summary",
                "label": "Summary"
              },
              "category": {
                "source": "build_draft.category",
                "label": "Category"
              },
              "severity": {
                "source": "build_draft.severity",
                "label": "Severity"
              },
              "priority": {
                "source": "build_draft.priority",
                "label": "Priority"
              },
              "sla": {
                "source": "build_draft.sla",
                "label": "SLA"
              },
              "owner": {
                "source": "build_draft.owner",
                "label": "Owner"
              }
            },
            "branches": [
              {
                "label": "Approve",
                "goto": "create_ticket"
              },
              {
                "label": "Reject",
                "goto": "reply_rejected"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "create_ticket",
          "next": "post_created",
          "type": "code",
          "config": {
            "name": "Create ticket (placeholder)",
            "code": "def run(inputs: Inputs) -> Outputs:\n    ref = \"TRIAGE-PENDING\"\n    lines = [\n        \"\ud83e\udd16 \u2705 Approved. Ticket created (placeholder \" + ref + \")\",\n        \"Title:    \" + (inputs.title or \"\").strip(),\n        \"Category: \" + (inputs.category or \"\").strip()\n        + \"   |   Severity: \" + (inputs.severity or \"\").strip()\n        + \"   |   Priority: \" + (inputs.priority or \"\").strip()\n        + \"   |   SLA: \" + (inputs.sla or \"\").strip(),\n        \"Owner:    \" + (inputs.owner or \"\").strip(),\n        \"Summary:  \" + (inputs.summary or \"\").strip(),\n        \"\",\n        \"(Jira not wired yet - this is the approved payload that will be sent to Jira.)\",\n    ]\n    return {\"response\": \"\\n\".join(lines)}\n",
            "input_fields": {
              "title": {
                "type": "string",
                "source": "build_draft.title"
              },
              "summary": {
                "type": "string",
                "source": "build_draft.summary"
              },
              "category": {
                "type": "string",
                "source": "build_draft.category"
              },
              "severity": {
                "type": "string",
                "source": "build_draft.severity"
              },
              "priority": {
                "type": "string",
                "source": "build_draft.priority"
              },
              "sla": {
                "type": "string",
                "source": "build_draft.sla"
              },
              "owner": {
                "type": "string",
                "source": "build_draft.owner"
              }
            },
            "output_fields": {
              "response": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "Created-ticket text for Teams"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "post_created",
          "next": "_end",
          "type": "tool",
          "config": {
            "name": "Post created ticket to Teams",
            "tool_name": "send_chat_message",
            "input_fields": {
              "chat_id": {
                "source": "input.conversation_id"
              },
              "content": {
